root, sudo and Least Privilege 
root is the account with UID 0. Permission checks are simply skipped for it. There is no file root cannot 
read, no process root cannot kill, and no safety net if root types the wrong command. 
For that reason, nobody sensible works as root. Instead, an ordinary user borrows root’s authority for 
one command at a time with sudo, which also writes a line to the system log every time it is used. 
Working as root all day is the equivalent of the hostel warden handing out the master key at the gate. 
