Ownership 
Every file and every directory carries two owners: a user owner, normally whoever created it, and a 
group owner. Permissions are then written separately for the user owner, for members of the 
owning group, and for everybody else. Those three audiences are traditionally abbreviated u, g and 
o, with a meaning all three at once. 
