Default Permissions and umask 
New files do not arrive with random permissions. The system starts from 666 for files and 777 for 
directories, then removes whatever the umask says to remove. A umask of 022 therefore produces 
644 files and 755 directories, which is what you saw in Lab 02. 
umask        # show the current mask 
umask 077    # new files become 600, new directories 700 
A umask of 077 is the right default on a shared or sensitive machine: everything you create is private 
until you deliberately open it. Note that changing it in a terminal lasts only for that terminal. 
